A||N||9||WoW||engine wap questions?||||5||
Z||000000||WoW||04-10-2001||02:23 PM||||well, i recently converted my fiero into the replica diablo and now planning to get a better engine. i was thnking about getting the chevy 454 vortec big block engine. has anyone ever done it? i want hp and of course TORQUE. Well, any replies or suggestions on which engine should be better will be helpful. thanks for your time.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Steven||04-10-2001||04:39 PM||||In 1997 GM rated the L29 Vortec 7400 (454) at 290hp @ 4000 rpm and 410lb @ 3200 rpm.<BR><P>------------------<BR> 85 Fiero GT<BR> 3.2 Liter Under Construction||||reg||1
Z||000002||KRMFiero||04-10-2001||04:44 PM||||Welcome to the forum, about the 454 its not possible (well maybe if you got 15,000$ and room to longitudaly mount the engine) If you want a GM vortec engine you would have to get a small block with one of Archie's kits. it would run great in your car.<P>Also you might want to think about Caddy V-8's the 4.5, 4.9 and Northstar engines are nice and have 200+ HP stock (I belive the northstar is 300 hp stock with out a chip or anything). Also the Northstar is a great looking and sounding engine!<P>One more swap you might want to look into is the GM 3800 Series II Supercharged V-6. if you change the pully on the blower you will get 270hp from one of these plus the have a higher redline then a v-8 (I belive).<BR> <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx" TARGET=_blank>http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx</A>  <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cwestco.com/</A>  <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/</A> <P>Kyle<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (Red)<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (White)<P>     <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/sig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dave Gunsul||04-10-2001||08:20 PM||||Actually it IS possible to<BR>put a 454 in a Fiero and <BR>without mounting it long.<BR>I have a copy of a F.O.C.O.A.<BR>magazine that shows a Fiero <BR>with a 454 and tunnel ram on it!<BR>Zumalt used to make a kit for<BR>big blocks but I have no idea where<BR>you can get them or if they are even<BR>still being sold. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000004||rockcrawl||04-10-2001||08:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>about the 454 its not possible (well maybe if you got 15,000$ and room to longitudaly mount the engine)<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Not true. In fact big block chevys have been mounted in Fieros transversly. Gary Zumalt used to sell a kit before he left the Fiero business a few years ago. One more point, mounting the engine longitudinally is far cheaper than using a transverse kit. That's the reason I did it with my 350. It just requires a little more fabrication and removal of the trunk. My total cost including the TPI engine and auto trans was less than Archies deluxe kit (no offense against you Archie  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ). All that said, I think the big block is a little too heavy for the Fiero.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cheever2||04-10-2001||08:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>no offense against you Archie<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>I don't think you have anything to worry about.  Once Arch saw the word "Zumalt" you can be pretty sure he ran outta here.  That's like yelling "Incoming".<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||WoW||04-10-2001||10:19 PM||||Everyone, thanks for the replies. I think it is possible because the bought my diablo kit from exotic rebodies and the person said that most people used the BMW 750series V12 engine and it fits perfectly with a little extra room. <BR>Well, I haven't decided which engine to get yet. Can someone please list different possible engines that's good for the fiero (remember I did a Diablo conversion) and also list the HP and lbs. of TORQUE. and I want TORQUE! =) Thanks again, really appreciate it.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Will||04-11-2001||02:47 PM||||This is first the question that should have asked:<P>Has your chassis been stretched to give the Diablo the correct wheelbase?<BR>Having a stretched chassis significantly improves your engine choices and their ease of installation.<BR>If you can get a V12 into that chassis, it is probably stretched. If you can get a V12 into that chassis, why are you asking about V8's? Although a V8 does have a LOT more performance potential for the dollar.<P>If it has, you might check out <A HREF="http://www.heldmotorsports.com" TARGET=_blank>www.heldmotorsports.com</A>  and look for their longitudinal cradles.<P>As far as engines go, check out <A HREF="http://www.gmpowertrain.com" TARGET=_blank>www.gmpowertrain.com</A>  for info on them.<P>It wouldn't exactly sound right, but you could put in GM's new 6.6 litre turbo diesel  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  300 HP and 520 ftlbs of torque, easy to get more because it's turbo.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Another option might be an old 500 cubic inch Cadillac. There's not much aftermarket available, but it's an excellent engine.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fierowrecker||04-11-2001||07:03 PM||||WOW!<BR>I would go with a small block chevy 350 out of a van or truck, with 4 bolt mains...<BR>Next, I would get the Systemax II to bump the HP to 425...<BR>The dollar to hp ratio is better with the chevy engine...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000009||Dave Gunsul||04-11-2001||08:52 PM||||I would suggest a small block too.<BR>A Fiero really doesn't need that much torque<BR>to get it moving becuase of it's light weight. besides, a big block would upset<BR>your handling. Get a machine shop to build<BR>a 350 with 9.5 comp., a 280 or close cam,<BR>Trick Flow 23 deg. alum. heads, and an Edel-<BR>brock manifold and you should be making<BR>400+ HP and 390-400+ Ib FT. That should move you nicely.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> You could put a dual quad<BR>manifold to be really different!<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
